===Verb===
{{en-verb|bites|biting|bit|bitten|past_ptc2=bit|past_ptc2_qual=rare}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cut into something by clamping the teeth.
#: {{ux|en|As soon as you '''bite''' that sandwich, you'll know how good it is.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To hold something by clamping one's teeth.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[attack]] with the [[teeth]].
#: {{ux|en|That dog is about to '''bite'''!}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To behave [[aggressive]]ly; to reject advances.
#: {{ux|en|If you see me, come and say hello. I don't '''bite'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[take hold]]; to [[establish]] [[firm]] [[contact]] with.
#: {{ux|en|I needed snow chains to make the tires '''bite'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To have significant effect, often negative.
#: {{ux|en|For homeowners with adjustable rate mortgages, rising interest will really '''bite'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a fish}} To bite a [[bait]]ed [[hook]] or other [[lure]] and thus be caught.
#: {{ux|en|Are the fish '''biting''' today?}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|metaphor}} To accept something offered, often secretly or deceptively, to cause some action by the acceptor.
#: {{ux|en|I've planted the story. Do you think they'll '''bite'''?}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|transitive|of an insect}} To [[sting]].
#: {{ux|en|These mosquitoes are really '''biting''' today!}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To cause a [[smart]]ing sensation; to have a property which causes such a sensation; to be [[pungent]].
#: {{ux|en|It '''bites''' like pepper or mustard.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|sometimes|figurative}} To cause sharp pain or damage to; to hurt or injure.
#: {{ux|en|Pepper '''bites''' the mouth.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|V|ii|229|1|passage={{...}}froſts doe '''bite''' the Meads{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To cause sharp pain; to produce anguish; to hurt or injure; to have the property of so doing.
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Proverbs|23|32|column=1|url=https://archive.org/details/Bible1611/page/n741/mode/1up|text=At the laſt it [wine] '''biteth''' like a ſerpent, and ſtingeth like ‖ an adder.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To take or keep a firm hold.
#: {{ux|en|The anchor '''bites'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take hold of; to hold fast; to adhere to.
#: {{ux|en|The anchor '''bites''' the ground.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Tale of Two Cities|Fire Rises|152|{{...}}the last screw of the rack having been turned so often that its purchase crumbled, and it now turned and turned with nothing to '''bite'''{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|slang}} To [[lack]] [[quality]]; to be worthy of [[derision]]; to [[suck]].
#: {{ux|en|This music really '''bites'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal|vulgar}} To perform [[oral sex]] on. {{non-gloss definition|Used in [[invective]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|You don't like that I sat on your car? '''Bite''' me.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|AAVE|slang}} To [[plagiarize]], to imitate.
#: {{ux|en|He always be '''biting''' my moves.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive|slang}} To [[deceive]] or [[defraud]]; to [[take in]]. <!--ref: Hotten's slang dict.-->

